 "_doc": "#1495 THE DECLARED MAPPING of the one hierarchy: tree node (the Cloud-C3 app's ui.sections as data/gen_c3_hierarchy.py reads it) -> the cloudy-c3-api route patterns and the cloudy-c3-mcp tool-name patterns it owns. Route patterns: `:` is one segment, a trailing `*` is the rest; tool patterns: exact legacy dotted name or a prefix ending in `*`. The most specific pattern wins, an overlap with the same specificity is an error, and every route and tool must be owned (guarded in cloudy-u-containers cloudy-c3-api/cloudy-c3-mcp tests and by test/test_c3_hierarchy.py). A page of the Containers section other than All is the same data scoped by project (`scoped`). `catalog_pages` are the pages that have no fragment of their own: they draw their API routes and MCP tools as OpsMap rows (maps.hier_<leaf id> of data/ops_maps.json, generated). Node ids are the app's page ids with the parent's `<parent>_` prefix dropped (ops/net/wg is net_wg). Edit this file and the app's build.json, then run data/gen_c3_hierarchy.py; never edit c3_hierarchy.json.",
